{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-19-1","title":"Job 19:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job, complaining of his friends' cruelty, shews there is misery enough in him to feed their cruelty. 21 He craves pity. 23 He believes the resurrection.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-2","title":"Job 19:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>How long. 8:2; 18:2; Ps 13:1; Re 6:10 vex. 27:2; Jud 16:16; Ps 6:2,3; 42:10; 2Pe 2:7,8 break me. Ps 55:21; 59:7; 64:3; Pr 12:18; 18:21; Jas 3:6-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-3","title":"Job 19:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>ten times. Ge 31:7; Le 26:26; Nu 14:22; Ne 4:12; Da 1:20 ye reproached. 4:6-11; 5:3,4; 8:4-6; 11:3,14; 15:4-6,11,12; 18:4-21 make yourselves strange to me. or, harden yourselves againstme. 17; Ge 42:7; Ps 69:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-4","title":"Job 19:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>I have erred. 11:3-6 mine. 2Sa 24:17; Pr 9:12; Eze 18:4; 2Co 5:10; Ga 6:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-5","title":"Job 19:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>magnify. Ps 35:26; 38:16; 41:11; 55:12; Mic 7:8; Zep 2:10; Zec 12:7 plead. 1Sa 1:6; Ne 1:3; Isa 4:1; Lu 1:25; 13:2-4; Joh 9:2,34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-6","title":"Job 19:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>God. 7:20; 16:11-14; Ps 44:9-14; 66:10-12 compassed. 18:8-10; La 1:12,13; Eze 12:13; 32:3; Ho 7:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-7","title":"Job 19:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I cry. 10:3,15-17; 16:17-19; 21:27; Ps 22:2; Jer 20:8; La 3:8; Hab 1:2,3 wrong. or, violence. no judgment. 9:32; 13:15-23; 16:21; 23:3-7; 31:35,36; 34:5; 40:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-8","title":"Job 19:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>fenced. 3:23; Ps 88:8; La 3:7,9; Ho 2:6 set. Jos 24:7; Pr 4:19; Isa 50:10; Jer 13:16; 23:12; Joh 8:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-9","title":"Job 19:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>stripped. 29:7-14,20,21; 30:1; Ps 49:16,17; 89:44; Isa 61:6; Ho 9:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-10","title":"Job 19:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>destroyed. 1:13-19; 2:7; Ps 88:13-18; La 2:5,6; 2Co 4:8,9 I am gone. 17:11; Ps 102:11 mine hope. 6:11; 8:13-18; 17:15; 24:20; Ps 37:35,36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-11","title":"Job 19:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>kindled. De 32:22; Ps 89:46; 90:7 he counteth. 13:24; 16:9; 33:10; La 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-12","title":"Job 19:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>His. 16:11; Isa 10:5,6; 51:23 raise. 30:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-13","title":"Job 19:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>put my brethren. Ps 31:11; 38:11; 69:8,20; 88:8,18; Mt 26:56; 2Ti 4:16 estranged. 6:21-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-14","title":"Job 19:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>kinsfolk. Ps 38:11; Pr 18:24; Mic 7:5,6; Mt 10:21 familiar. 2Sa 16:23; Ps 55:12-14; Jer 20:10; Joh 13:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-15","title":"Job 19:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>dwell. 16-19 count me. 31:31,32; Ps 123:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-16","title":"Job 19:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>my servant. 1:15,16,17,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-17","title":"Job 19:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>breath. 2:9,10; 17:1 body. Heb. belly.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-18","title":"Job 19:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Yea. 30:1,12; 2Ki 2:23; Isa 3:5 young children. or, the wicked.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-19","title":"Job 19:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>my inward friends. Heb. the men of my secret. Ps 41:9; 55:12-14,20 they whom. 6:14,15; Ps 109:4,5; Lu 22:48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-20","title":"Job 19:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>bone. 30:30; 33:19-22; Ps 22:14-17; 32:3,4; 38:3; 102:3,5; La 4:8 and to. or, as. and I am. 2:4-6; 7:5; La 3:4; 5:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-21","title":"Job 19:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>have pity. 6:14; Ro 12:15; 1Co 12:26; Heb 13:3 the hand. 1:11; 2:5,10; 6:4; Ps 38:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-22","title":"Job 19:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>persecute. 10:16; 16:13,14; Ps 69:26 and are not. 2:5; 31:31; Isa 51:23; Mic 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-23","title":"Job 19:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Oh. Heb. Who will give, etc. my words. 31:35; Isa 8:1; 30:8 oh that they were.Rather, \"Oh that they were described {yuchakoo} in a book, with an iron stile and lead! Were graven on a rock for ever!\" Pliny observes, \"At first men wrote on palm leaves, and afterwards on the bark or rind of other trees. In process of time, public monuments were written on rolls of lead ({plumbeis voluminibus}); and those of a private nature on linen books, or tables covered with wax.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-24","title":"Job 19:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>graven. Ex 28:11,12,21; 32:16; De 27:2,3,8; Jer 17:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-25","title":"Job 19:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>I know. 33:23,24; Ps 19:14; Isa 54:5; 59:20,21; Eph 1:7 he shall. Ge 3:15; 22:18; Joh 5:22-29; Jude 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-26","title":"Job 19:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>And though, etc.Or, After I shall awake, though this body be destroyed, yet out of my flesh shall I see God.</p>\n<p>Ps 17:15 in my flesh. Ps 16:9,11; Mt 5:8; 1Co 13:12; 15:53; Php 3:21; 1Jo 3:2; Re 1:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-27","title":"Job 19:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>I shall. Nu 24:17; Isa 26:19 another. Heb. a stranger. though my reins, etc. or, myreins within me are consumed with earnest desire [for that day.] Ps 119:81; Php 1:23 within me. Heb. in my bosom.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-28","title":"Job 19:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Why. 22; Ps 69:26 seeing, etc. or, and what root of matter is found in me?the root. 1Ki 14:13 in me.Instead of {bee,} \"in me,\" {bo,} \"in him,\" is the reading of more than 100 MSS.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-19-29","title":"Job 19:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>ye afraid. 13:7-11; Ro 13:1-4 that ye may. Ps 58:10,11; Ec 11:9; Mt 7:1,2; Jas 4:11,12</p>"}]}